module gunbc.live_deploy.intent

import std.types { String }
import gunbc.live_deploy.release_locus { ReleaseRevisionBinding }

// WHICH ROLL-OUT A DEPLOYMENT ACT OWNS, said once at the top of the act instead of re-derived at
// every link. The target architecture (manager frame, operator-endorsed) is ONE live_deploy
// convergence owning the COMPLETE revision artifact closure -- source snapshot, binary, helper
// snapshots with reproducible receipts, generated units, generated config, secret refs, and a
// manifest -- parameterized by this intent, with environments differing by data and policy only and
// a branch never being an artifact's identity (a branch may SELECT a revision; the revision is the
// identity). This record lands WITH its first consumer (DESIGN §3c: no standalone type ahead of the
// work that reads it): the attempt-unit helper-closure verify in gunbc.live_deploy.apply_legs
// attempt_helper_snapshot_verify_leg, which turns the 127-failing drain of the lab's hand deploys
// (the drain unit named /opt/gunbc/attempt-system-unit-helpers/<instance>/<rev>/ while nothing had
// installed it) into a refusal at apply time, before any unit that names the locus is enabled.
//
// FIELD DISCIPLINE: environment, entry, targets, configuration and rollout policy join this record
// exactly when a slice reads them -- S1 consumes the instance and the revision, so S1 declares the
// instance and the revision. An unreader field is a dangling declaration wearing a load-bearing
// name, and the seed's refusal is the least of its problems.

data DeploymentIntent {
  instance_id: String
  revision: ReleaseRevisionBinding
}
